          <attvalue for="36" value="A rise in the policy rate raises corporate borrowing costs and hurdle rates for capital projects, prompting European auto and tech firms (and their financiers) to delay or cancel factory and capacity investments, reducing manufacturing investment flows within the next cycle." />
