          <attvalue for="35" value="0.8" />
          <attvalue for="36" value="A sustained rise in the policy rate increases real borrowing costs and signals stronger anti-inflation policy, directly lowering market and survey inflation expectations as agents revise demand and wage growth outlooks." />
